    <node id="10 000 000 FT-IG">
      <data key="d0">ÖSSZEGHATÁR</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity **“10 000 000 FT-IG”** refers to a set of financial thresholds applying to various procurement, contractual, and settlement-related procedures. It marks the upper limit up to which several matters may be handled under simplified decision-making and preparatory rules. These include communication and marketing commitments, where different approval and preparation roles apply below this amount, as well as other revenue-related financial commitments that follow simpler procedural rules under the threshold.

For asset-related transactions, **10 000 000 FT-IG** is an important value limit in multiple contexts. It applies to the sale of movable property, where procedures are valid up to a value of 10 million forints, and to the purchase of assets connected to real estate, which may be managed under a simpler decision order when below this amount. It also covers investment and operating contracts related to a given property, which may follow a simplified approval process up to this financial threshold.

In legal and settlement matters, **10 000 000 FT-IG** serves as the financial ceiling for out-of-court settlements, waivers of claims, and compensation agreements. It also defines a threshold below which special approval and decision rules apply, particularly in the procurement of legal advisory services.

Overall, **10 000 000 FT-IG** is a comprehensive financial limit used to distinguish lower-value cases that can be handled through simplified internal procedures from those requiring more formal decision-making and authorization.</data>
      <data key="d2">9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEM RELEVÁNS">
      <data key="d0">ÖSSZEGHATÁR</data>
      <data key="d1">A **NEM RELEVÁNS** megjelölés azt jelzi, hogy az adott stratégiai megállapodásoknál, illetve kötelezettségvállalási tárgynál **nem alkalmazandó összeghatár vagy értékhatár szerinti korlátozás**. A 12.1. sorban szereplő összeghatár-megjelölés alapján ez azt fejezi ki, hogy az érintett esetben **nincs meghatározott limit**, ezért az adott szabályozási vagy eljárási rendelkezés szempontjából az értékhatár nem releváns.</data>
